			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Drive extension-host API fidelity across twelve subsystems\n\nReplace no-op stubs and plain-object placeholders with real implementations across twelve VS Code API subsystems, closing gaps that silently broke extensions relying on standard `vscode` namespace contracts:\n\n- **EnvironmentVariableCollection** (`ActivateExtension`): Replace the previous no-op stub with a mutation-tracking implementation that forwards `replace`, `append`, `prepend`, `delete`, `clear` operations to Mountain via `terminal.envCollection.*` notifications. Cross-session persistence is delegated to Mountain's global memento. Extensions (Copilot, GitHub PR, Pyright) that inject PATH/auth tokens into terminal environments now see their vars applied.\n\n- **Storage cache priming** (`ActivateExtension`): Pre-populate `workspaceState` and `globalState` caches BEFORE `activate()` runs via a single `Storage.GetItems` round-trip, partitioned by extension-prefixed keys. Synchronous reads inside activate (Roo Code's `taskHistory`, Copilot's `signInDismissed`, GitLens welcome state) return real values instead of defaults, preventing UI state regressions after reload.\n\n- **Extension descriptor fidelity** (`ActivateExtension`): Use `MakeUri()` for `extension.extensionUri` so `.with()` / `.toString()` work (Roo Code, Continue, Claude all resolve bundled assets this way); add real `activate()` returning a resolving promise; set `extensionKind: 1` (UI).\n\n- **Text editor commands** (`Commands/Namespace`): `registerTextEditorCommand` now drives the callback inside `editor.edit()` so the real TextEditorEdit buffer applies atomically. Refactor, sort-lines, and Cmd+I previously collected edits into a no-op builder.\n\n- **Language provider metadata** (`Languages/Namespace`): Forward `documentSelector` (full array), `triggerCharacters`, `providedCodeActionKinds`, `firstTriggerCharacter`/`moreTriggerCharacter` to Mountain so Monaco invokes providers at the correct moments — completions on `.`, signature-help on `(`, on-type formatting on `;`, ESLint quick-fixes under the right menu. Handle both varargs and metadata-object overloads for `registerSignatureHelpProvider`. Update `Document.languageId` in-place in `setTextDocumentLanguage`.\n\n- **Task executions** (`Tasks/Namespace`): `executeTask` now returns a real `{ task, terminate() }` object. `taskExecutions` is a live getter reflecting the current active execution set, driven by `task.didStart` / `task.didEnd` notifications from Mountain.\n\n- **LogOutputChannel** (`Window/CreateOutputChannel`): Full `LogOutputChannel` implementation with ISO-8601 timestamped level-prefixed output, log-level filtering (`trace`/`debug`/`info`/`warn`/`error`), `onDidChangeLogLevel` listener support, proper `show(preserveFocus)` overload, atomic `replace()`, and dispose-time listener cleanup.\n\n- **Status bar items** (`Window/CreateStatusBarItem`): Support `createStatusBarItem(id, alignment?, priority?)` overload (1.74+), proper command object normalisation, accessibility information forwarding, idempotent `dispose()` guard, and change-deduplication.\n\n- **Terminal state** (`Window/CreateTerminal`): Track `state.isInteractedWith` from Mountain notifications, expose `exitStatus` getter, default `addNewLine` to true in `sendText` (appending `\\r`) so typed commands auto-execute.\n\n- **Webview panel** (`Window/CreateWebviewPanel`): Complete rewrite with proper getter/setter pattern, live `viewColumn`/`active`/`visible` via per-handle `webview.viewState` bridge, idempotent `DisposeInternal()` with emitter cleanup, `onDidDispose`/`onDidChangeViewState` listener arrays, iconPath forwarding, and forward-reference pattern to break TDZ cycles.\n\n- **Tree data providers** (`Window/Namespace`): Subscribe to `onDidChangeTreeData` on both `createTreeView` and `registerTreeDataProvider` so Mountain/Sky refresh on extension-driven tree mutations. Proper disposal cleanup on `TreeView.dispose()` and the returned disposable.\n\n- **WebviewView provider** (`Window/Namespace`): Forward `retainContextWhenHidden` option to Mountain so Roo/Continue/Claude sidebar views preserve React state across panels.\n\n- **Status bar messages** (`Window/Namespace`): `setStatusBarMessage` now supports all three upstream overloads — persist-until-disposed, timed auto-hide via `setTimeout`, and thenable-resolved hide. Returns a `dispose()` function that actually clears.\n\n- **Filesystem write encoding** (`Workspace/File/System/Namespace`): Send binary content as a `Uint8Array` → `number[]` instead of UTF-8 decoded text, preventing corruption of PNG, zip, and BOM-prefixed writes from image-processing and archive extensions.\n\n- **applyEdit return value** (`Workspace/Text/Document`): Return Mountain's actual success boolean instead of always `true`, so format-on-save / organize-imports / rename-refactor can retry or surface errors on failure.\n\n- **Per-subsystem routing tiers** (`Bootstrap/Main`, `Utility/Tier`): Add `__LandTier_*` esbuild defines and `__LandTiers` registration for 15 subsystems (Terminal, SCM, Debug, LanguageFeatures, Search, OutputChannel, NativeHost, TreeView, Storage, Model, Tasks, Auth, Encryption, ExtensionHost, WebSocket) with type definitions and defaults matching `.env.Land` profiles.\n\n- **Route manifest** (`Generated/RouteManifest`): Add generated three-tier route hierarchy (`MountainMethods`, `StockLiftExports`, `BespokeCocoonMethods`) with summary banner for boot-time diagnostics.\n\nTogether these changes resolve roughly a dozen classes of silent extension breakage across AI assistants, language tooling, source control, and debugger integrations.",
