			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Inline DAP adapters and webview panel persistence\n\nImplement three extension-host fidelity improvements that close gaps between Cocoon and VS Code's extension API surface:\n\n- **Inline DAP adapters (`DebugAdapterInlineImplementation`)**: Track `debug.didStartSession`/`didTerminateSession` events from Mountain to instantiate per-session adapters in-process. Wire `onDidSendMessage` back to Mountain via `debug.dap-response` and dispatch incoming DAP frames from the `ExtHostDebug$sendDAPRequest` gRPC handler. Adapter factories are stashed in `ExtensionRegistry` by debug type for reverse-RPC lookup.\n\n- **Webview panel serialization**: Implement `registerWebviewPanelSerializer` to register serializers via `ExtensionRegistry`. Handle `ExtHostWebviewPanels$serializeAllWebviewPanels` and `$deserializeWebviewPanel` gRPC methods so extension panels (Live Preview, AI chat, custom editors) survive `nativeHost:reload`.\n\n- **Document state tracking**: Update `version` and `isDirty` on `$acceptDocumentChanged` and after document-save notifications in HandleSpecificNotification so extensions reading `document.version` and `document.isDirty` see correct values.\n\nAlso fix `BuildGetConfiguration` to return the caller's `DefaultValue` when Mountain signals \"no override\" (null), matching VS Code's configuration model where null means \"use default\".\n\nRemove stale `Source/Generated/RouteManifest.*` artifacts.",
			"SHA": "3f6d788763197e17a379582d325c7449754b615f"
		},
